{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Review UK 1965 independence referendum refusal for Mauritius & Chagos detachment",
        "additional_details": "Paragraph 17 of the 1965 Constitutional Conference report records the British Secretary of State rejecting a referendum. We believe the 1967 election was not a referendum on the 1965 detachment and that the people across then British Mauritius deserved a direct say. \r\n \r\nThe review should examine consent, pressure and representation, and hear affected communities. We seek accountability and respect for self-determination.",
        "background": "Commission an independent review of the UK\u2019s rejection of an independence referendum for Mauritius and decision to detach the Chagos Islands from Mauritius. We want the Government to publish the review\u2019s findings and lay them before Parliament.",
